dialect grammar
grammar stdio.pptx.mutations
extension pptx
start document
comment none

# 🧬 Real one-line `OpText::print_op`/`parse_op` shape: `../../../🧬️schema/🦀️.rs`'s `PptxMutationRecord`
# (`#[derive(dsl::DslRecord)]` with `kind: String`, `value: dsl::DslValue`), printed through `dsl::print(.., JoinMode::Inline)`.
# The keyword-per-variant form this file used to describe belonged to the hand-written
# `print_pptx_mutation`, which the record derive replaced -- the printer wins, so this grammar
# restates the record: a `kind` tag, then the generic `DslValue` payload as the rest of the single physical line. Same honest restatement the
# sibling `🎒️zip` artifact's own mutations grammar already uses for the same generic codec.
document = "kind" "=" kind-tag "value" "=" REST

# `"mutation"` carries the tagged `PptxMutation` value in `value=`.
kind-tag = "mutation"
